# CPSC 462 — build products only. ONE file at course level, not one per kind:
# hw/, qz/ and exam/ have identical needs and three copies drift.
#
# Verify any change to this file with:  git check-ignore -v <path>

# --- LaTeX intermediates -----------------------------------------------------
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk

# --- flattened self-contained copies for Overleaf ----------------------------
# Generated output. The .tex sources beside them are tracked.
overleaf/

# --- compiled PDFs -----------------------------------------------------------
# Named for what WE build, not "*.pdf" with negations for what we don't.
#
# build_tex.sh writes <basename>.pdf beside each .tex, and every .tex in an
# assignment folder is either pNN_<slug>.tex or <kind>NN_solutions.tex. So these
# two patterns are exactly our build products and nothing else.
#
# A blanket "*.pdf" plus "!HW*.pdf" negations was the old rule, and it fails the
# wrong way: it silently untracks any instructor handout whose name was not
# guessed in advance -- and this course's handouts are named "Lab 0",
# "Introduction to Wireshark", "Hands on", none of which match HW*. Source
# material going missing is worse than a stray build product showing up in
# git status, so the rule is a whitelist of our own output.
p[0-9][0-9]_*.pdf
*_solutions.pdf

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   class_materials/*.pdf   instructor slide decks and syllabus -- source
#   hw*/,qz*/,exam*/ *.pdf  the instructor's assignment handout -- source
#   *.pcapng, *.pcap        packet captures this course may ship -- source,
#                           not a build product; keep them with the solution
